The host platform's os constraint comes from this extension, which reads the
JVM's os.name.  On MidnightBSD that is "midnightbsd", which matches nothing, so
the host platform carries no os constraint and every select() falls to its
linux default: the build stops in unix_jni_linux.cc for want of sys/xattr.h
(run 35745771678).  It is a FreeBSD derivative and its packages are the FreeBSD
builds, so answer freebsd.  CI only.

diff -u -r a/host/extension.bzl b/host/extension.bzl
--- a/host/extension.bzl
+++ b/host/extension.bzl
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 def _translate_os(os):
     if os.startswith("mac os"):
         return "osx"
+    if os.startswith("midnightbsd"):
+        return "freebsd"
     if os.startswith("freebsd"):
         return "freebsd"
     if os.startswith("openbsd"):
